Z||000003||strdream||11-11-2000||08:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FIEROCIOUS:<BR><B>Welcome! I told you about the forum also! <P>I took your advice and desided not to get the V8 adapter plate. After all, if I can't take the cosequences of modifying a car then why modify them! <P>After 10+ years and being an ASE master tech and all, my modifying days are over!<P>I took your letter rather insultive! I don't think I should consider not modifying cars because I had a simple question about the longevity of your buisness, and the availability of parts after you deside to quit produceing Fiero products!<P>At least V8 Archie has been around a while!   </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Oh hi Mike<BR>I remember you telling me about the Forum, I just didn't think of it than. Sorry if you felt insulted by my e-mail, I didn't think you where talking about my future in business, I thought you where refering the future of radical high performance stuff and swaping V8s in Fieros. I know a guy not far from me here in Michigan that loves to punch the ponies out with the V6s and race poeple with their new Corvettes and blow 'em away in his Fiero.  <P>||||reg||1
